72.text:
 One JSON object per line: {"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"head","seq":0,"head":{"headers":[["content-type","application/json"]],"method":"POST","url":"https://api.example.com/v1/x"}}
{"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"data","seq":1,"data":"aGVsbG8="}
{"flow":"01J9…","dir":"request","kind":"end","seq":2,"bytes":5} fieldmeaningflowthe exchange's id in the flow logdirrequest or responsekindhead, data (body bytes, base64), truncated (max_capture_body_bytes reached; nothing more is recorded) or end (with the total bytes, and aborted: true if the body did not complete)seqthe record's position for this flow and direction A body is its data records joined in seq order. Each data record
holds at most 48 KiB of body, so lines stay under 64 KiB plus a little
JSON, apart from head lines, which can be up to limits.max_header_bytes.

112.text:
 POST /roxy/v1/enrol with the enrolment token. {
  "roxy_version": "0.1.0",
  "protocol_version": 1
} fieldmeaningroxy_versionthe node's roxy versionprotocol_version1 {
  "node_id": "node-7f3a9c",
  "token": "nt1-9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",
  "not_after": "2026-11-05T10:12:00Z",
  "renew_after_seconds": 1296000
} fieldmeaningnode_idchosen by the server: 1 to 128 characters from A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -, fixed for the life of the nodetokenthe node token: 1 to 512 characters valid in a bearer token. The node stores it and sends it unchangednot_afterwhen the server stops accepting the token, in UTCrenew_after_secondswhen the node should renew the token, counted from when it received it. The node renews no later than two thirds of the way to not_after whatever this says The control plane decides how long tokens last and how it stores them.
We recommend single-use enrolment tokens with a short expiry, and storing
node tokens hashed. The node keeps its token in its state dir (mode
0600).

114.text:
 POST /roxy/v1/lease with the node token. The body reports the node's
state: {
  "lease_id": "lease-01J9Z8K3",
  "roxy_version": "0.1.0",
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "uptime_seconds": 86400,
  "policy_state": "loaded",
  "spooled_bytes": 0,
  "seq_unreserved": false,
  "quarantine": null
} fieldmeaninglease_idthe lease the node has applied, or null before the first. A node that reports an old lease_id did not apply the latest leasepolicy_statenone (no lease yet), loaded or expiredspooled_bytesflow-log data waiting to be acknowledgedseq_unreservedtrue if the node cannot save its flow sequence counter, so a restart might reuse sequence numbers. A node that reports this for long needs its state dir looked atquarantinethe node's quarantine, or null {
  "id": "q-01J9ZB7QX4R2M8K3N5P6T7V8W9",
  "since": "2026-10-13T09:14:02Z",
  "cause": {"kind": "rule", "rule": "exfil-guard", "flow": "01J9ZB7P"}
} fieldmeaningidthe incident's id, which a release must namesincewhen it was tripped, by the node's clockcausewhat tripped it: kind: rule with the rule and flow, kind: threshold with the listener and its threshold, or kind: layer with the layer and flow The server answers 200 with the whole lease on every poll, or an
error.

115.text:
 {
  "lease_id": "lease-01J9Z8K3",
  "valid_for_seconds": 900,
  "refresh_after_seconds": 300,
  "config": "version: 1\nlisteners:\n  - name: proxy\n    bind: 0.0.0.0:8080\nsecrets:\n  github: { lease: true }\nrules:\n  - id: github\n    when: host == \"api.github.com\"\n    then: [allow]\n",
  "secrets": {
    "github": "ghp_example"
  },
  "state_epoch": "2026-10-06T09:00:00Z",
  "flow": {
    "ship": true,
    "batch_max_bytes": 1048576,
    "flush_interval_seconds": 5,
    "spool_high_water_bytes": 67108864,
    "on_high_water": "hold"
  },
  "quarantine": {
    "release": ["q-01J9ZB7QX4R2M8K3N5P6T7V8W9"]
  }
} fieldmeaninglease_idany string that changes whenever anything else in the lease changesvalid_for_secondshow long the lease is valid, measured by the node's own clock from just before it sent the request. Clock differences between the node and server do not matterrefresh_after_secondswhen to poll next. Leave room for several retries; a third of valid_for_seconds is reasonable. The node polls no later than halfway through the leaseconfiga complete roxy.yaml. Secrets the lease supplies are declared as name: { lease: true }secretsthe value of each lease: true secretstate_epochany string. When it changes, the node clears all rule state and metric counts before applying the lease, which is how a control plane lifts a lockout a rule imposedflowhow to send the flow log (flow upload). ship: false turns it off. on_high_water says what happens when spool_high_water_bytes are waiting: hold holds traffic, spool drops the oldest eventsquarantineoptional. release lists the quarantine ids the control plane has released. The node lifts its quarantine when its id is listedinterception_careserved; not sent by a v1 server The node applies a lease in full or not at all. A lease whose config
roxy check would reject, or that lacks a secret the config declares, is
logged and ignored, and the node keeps the lease it has. A change to
secrets alone is applied without reloading the rest of the policy.

178.text:
 A WASM addon is a WebAssembly component. Write one in Rust with the
roxy-addon
SDK: use roxy_addon::prelude::*;

struct RedactTokens;
impl Layer for RedactTokens {
    fn init(_config: &str) -> Result<Self, String> {   // the addon's `config:`, as JSON
        Ok(RedactTokens)
    }
    fn handle(&mut self, req: Request, next: Next) -> Response {
        let req = req.map_body(|body| body.transform(redact_chunk));
        next.run(req)
    }
}
roxy_addon::export!(RedactTokens); handle runs once per exchange. It can change the request, call
next.run to pass it on and get the response, or answer the client
itself.Body streams: read it as it arrives with transform (per chunk) or
pipe (with state, able to hold bytes back), or collect it with
read_to_end(cap).flow::* and call_endpoint reach roxy's
host services: tags, state, records, and
calls to configured endpoints.A panic fails the exchange closed.WebSockets need nothing extra: the request and response bodies carry
them. The test component
redact
is a complete streaming redactor.
